        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Should a Steward be required to leave the job to handle a grievance, he or she shall first secure the permission of his or her immediate Supervisor, informing the Supervisor as to the Departmental area of the grievance; and shall report to his or her Supervisor upon returning to work. When a Steward fulfills the conditions of this Section E, permission for him or her to leave his or her job to handle a grievance shall not be unreasonably withheld.",
            "block_bbox": [
                113,
                208,
                735,
                345
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    113.0,
                    208.0
                ],
                [
                    735.0,
                    208.0
                ],
                [
                    735.0,
                    345.0
                ],
                [
                    113.0,
                    345.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. In the event it is necessary under the provisions of the Grievance Procedure, and in accordance with the Letter of Certification, for a Steward to handle a grievance in a Department other than his or her own, he or she shall also report to the Foreman or Supervisor of such other Department immediately upon arrival there, and upon departure there from.",
            "block_bbox": [
                111,
